    "reasoning": "Every selected answer agrees with its own captured Math Academy worked solution. Independently: q-8008 gives x²=9 after substituting y=1; q-8005 gives y²=81/16 after substituting x=5. For q-71982, the modulus is 4 and the quadrant-II angle is 2π/3. For q-8077, the modulus is 2√2 and an angle is 7π/4. The diagram for q-71974 shows (-4,-4), giving modulus 4√2 and angle 5π/4. The diagram for q-17513 shows (3,2), giving modulus √13 and angle arctan(2/3)=0.588 radians to three decimal places. These exponential forms use angles modulo 2π. For q-40790, r=8 is the origin-centered circle of radius 8, matching option 4. For q-120156, the displayed radius is 2/3. For q-120182, the radius is √((-1)²+4²)=√17. For q-84699, the area scale factor is |48−28|=20. For q-164170, the disk has radius 3 and the determinant is −2, so its image area is 2·9π=18π. For q-9298, the triangle has area 1/2 and the determinant is 1, preserving that area. The positive amplitudes for q-80131, q-80126, and q-11295 are respectively √(16+1)=√17, √(7+9)=4, and √(4+9)=√13. For q-124143, substituting u=2 and v=−2 gives x=6 and y=−5. No mathematical disagreement with the captured answers was found.",
